From c42bf2debd7add325fc66099a02edd15c8020b3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Boris=20Sta=CC=88heli?= <ich@bstaehe.li>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:00:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] User button actions: melodies take priority, count-up to
 shutdown

- A press that starts while a melody plays (external notification nag
  or the hint tune) only stops it, right at button-down: the nag is
  acknowledged with the ack text, the hint tune is just stopped. The
  gesture of that press or click series is then ignored: no alert, no
  hint tune and no shutdown.
- With long_press_shutdown_ms set, the stock lead-up is replaced by a
  slowly rising count-up (8 notes, about one per second) from
  hold_alert_max_ms to the shutdown time; it stops on release. The
  schedule is a pure, tested helper.
- hold_alert_max_ms defaults to 3000.
- Default texts are written as "\x07" "HELP" so the bell never merges
  with the text into one hex escape.
